# Routing — ts_routes Only

All URLs must use typed helpers generated by `ts_routes` gem. Never write path strings manually.

Generate routes: `docker compose exec web bundle exec rake ts:routes`
Output: `app/frontend/shared/api/routes.ts`

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — typed, refactor-safe, compile-time checked
import Routes from 'shared/routes'

<Link href={Routes.companySessionPath(session.id)}>View</Link>
router.visit(Routes.companyProjectPath(project.id))
await apiFetch(Routes.terminalSessionsPath(), { method: 'POST', ... })

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded strings, no type safety, breaks silently
<Link href={`/company/sessions/${session.id}`}>View</Link>
router.visit(`/company/projects/${project.id}`)
await apiFetch('/terminal_sessions', { method: 'POST', ... })
```

When adding new Rails routes, regenerate TS helpers before using them on the frontend.
